:[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M18 20a6 6 0 0 0-12 0"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"12","cy":"10","r":"4"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"},"children":[]}]},{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Sign in to sync"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"main","props":{"className":"life-reader life-tip-layout"},"children":[{"tag":"aside","props":{"className":"life-reader-sidebar life-tip-sidebar"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"className":"life-back-link","href":"/en/book/12"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-left","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m12 19-7-7 7-7"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M19 12H5"},"children":[]}]},"Back to index"]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-sidebar-caption"},"children":["Starting a business: how to protect your personal assets"]},{"tag":"nav","props":{"aria-label":"Chapter entries"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-01"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["01"]},"Only invest money you can afford to lose — never use family savings or borrowed funds"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-02"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["02"]},"Never sign personal guarantees for corporate loans; spouses should definitely avoid signing too"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-03"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["03"]},"Choosing the right legal entity before launching: sole proprietors and general partners are fully liable, while limited liability companies offer “limited” liability"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-04"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["04"]},"Improperly listed shareholders: never hold shares on someone else’s behalf"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-05"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["05"]},"Check the Ministry of Commerce records before signing; obtain written disclosures and include a “cooling-off period” in the contract"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-06"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["06"]},"Determine the business name, location, scope of operations, and registered capital before registration; with complete documents, you can obtain the business license on the spot"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-07"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["07"]},"Businesses requiring licenses must wait until they obtain one"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-08"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["08"]},"Figure out which category you fall into: producing or preparing food requires a permit, selling only pre-packaged goods needs a filing, while selling fresh meat and vegetables needs no permit at all"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-09"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["09"]},"Packaging food for sale makes it prepackaged food: labels must include production date, shelf life, and ingredient list without exception"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-10"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["10"]},"General foods must not claim therapeutic effects: this applies to labels, instructions, ads, and live-stream scripts alike"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-11"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["11"]},"The food industry faces criminal penalties: selling meat from diseased animals or products exceeding safety limits is already a crime; adding toxic or harmful non-food substances carries a minimum five-year sentence regardless of revenue"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-12"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["12"]},"Once you obtain a business license, you must file tax returns on schedule — even if you have no income, you still need to submit a return with all zeros"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-13"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["13"]},"Invoices must reflect actual transactions; small taxpayers can fully utilize tax exemptions"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-14"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["14"]},"Scammers pretending to be tax officials demanding payments are fraudsters; tax filings must be done via the e-Tax Service or by calling 12366"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"aria-current":"page","className":"active","href":"/en/tip/12-15","data-status":"active"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["15"]},"Writing “deposit” instead of “advance payment” in contracts, specifying penalty amounts, and treating credit terms as loans"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-16"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["16"]},"Sign a written contract within the first month of employment; register for social insurance within 30 days"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-17"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["17"]},"Wages must be paid according to contracts and laws; raises, loans, and bonuses all require written documentation"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-18"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["18"]},"Sell first, then produce: use pre-orders and small orders to confirm demand before investing in manufacturing"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-19"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["19"]},"Run the prototype through the production checklist before starting full production"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-20"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["20"]},"Keep copies of invoices and supplier documentation for every shipment; avoid purchasing goods priced significantly below market rates: if an employee buys counterfeit products, the employer can still be held legally responsible"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-21"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["21"]},"Whether creating designs yourself or purchasing licensed artwork, simply changing colors or adding icons does not count as “modifications” for copyright purposes"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-22"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["22"]},"Follow procedures at work; think carefully about who bears responsibility before offering unsolicited help"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-23"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["23"]},"Exit the process as planned when losses occur: opt for simplified deregistration when possible, or file for bankruptcy if debts exceed assets — don’t leave things unattended"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-24"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["24"]},"Before paying for third‑party store management, e‑commerce training, or “dropshipping” services, be sure to ask whether extra fees will be required and where the sales figures actually come from"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/12-25"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["25"]},"Companies and individual businesses in China must report the previous year online from January 1 to June 30, even without business activity; annual reports are free"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-tip-page"},"children":[{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-breadcrumb","aria-label":"Breadcrumb"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book"},"children":["Explore the book"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"aria-hidden":"true"},"children":["/"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book/12"},"children":["Chapter 12"," ·"," ","Starting a business: how to protect your personal assets"]}]},{"tag":"article","props":{"className":"life-entry-card status-unmarked is-standalone","id":"12-15"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-top"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-entry-number"},"children":["15"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-evidence grade-a"},"children":["Evidence"," ","A"]}]},{"tag":"h1","props":{"lang":"en"},"children":["Writing “deposit” instead of “advance payment” in contracts, specifying penalty amounts, and treating credit terms as loans"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"lang":"en","className":"life-entry-summary"},"children":["Only when the word “deposit” is used does the double‑return rule apply: if you break the contract, you lose that money; if the other party breaks it, they must pay you twice the amount. Anything above 20% of the contract value does not qualify as a deposit. If you write “advance payment” instead, the law offers no such protection. Offering credit terms is essentially lending your own money to the buyer interest‑free; if they go bankrupt, it becomes a bad debt."]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-impact"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["No cost at all. Simply include the term “deposit” in the c…"]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["A deposit only becomes valid once the money is actually received by the seller (the effective date is when del…"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-actions","aria-label":"Mark: Writing “deposit” instead of “advance payment” in contracts, specifying penalty amounts, and treating credit terms as loans"},"children":[{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action done","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-check","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M20 6 9 17l-5-5"},"children":[]}]},"Done"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action todo","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-list-todo","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"rect","props":{"x":"3","y":"5","width":"6","height":"6","rx":"1"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m3 17 2 2 4-4"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 6h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 12h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 18h8"},"children":[]}]},"Plan to do"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action favorite","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-bookmark","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m19 21-7-4-7 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h10a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v16z"},"children":[]}]},"Save"]}," ",{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"social-share-trigger"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-share2 lucide-share-2","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"5","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"6","cy":"12","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"19","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"8.59","x2":"15.42","y1":"13.51","y2":"17.49"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"15.41","x2":"8.59","y1":"6.51","y2":"10.49"},"children":[]}]},"Share this tip"]}]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-detail-toggle","aria-expanded":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"10","height":"10","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"currentColor","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-circle","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"},"children":[]}]},"Hide details"]},{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-chevron-down rotated","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m6 9 6 6 6-6"},"children":[]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-details"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["No cost at all. Simply include the term “deposit” in the contract; the amount must not exceed 20% of the total contract value. Collect the payment before delivering goods. Before agreeing to any credit terms that let the buyer receive goods first and pay later, run a background check on them first."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["A deposit only becomes valid once the money is actually received by the seller (the effective date is when delivery occurs). If the buyer breaks the contract, they forfeit the deposit. If the seller breaks it, they must return the full amount plus an equal sum as compensation (i.e., double the original amount). Portions exceeding 20% of the total contract value are not treated as deposits. Should the agreed penalty amount be far higher or lower than the actual loss, a court may adjust it at the request of either party. When both a deposit and a penalty clause are included in the same contract, the injured party may claim only one of them, not both (nationwide, effective since 2021)."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Original sources"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":["全国人大 (2020). 民法典（第五百八十五、五百八十六、五百八十七、五百八十八条）. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.spp.gov.cn/spp/fl/202006/t20200602_463888.shtml","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://www.spp.gov.cn/spp/fl/202006/t20200602_463888.shtml"]}]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.spp.gov.cn/spp/fl/202006/t20200602_463888.shtml","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"life-source-link"},"children":["Open source link"," ",{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"13","height":"13","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-external-link","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M15 3h6v6"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M10 14 21 3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"},"children":[]}]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Book note"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-content-reference"},"children":["Under the Civil Code, “advance payment” does not enjoy the same protections as a deposit; it is generally regarded as a simple prepayment. This is the prevailing practice in legal practice, though no specific court rulings were verified for this section. Providing credit terms is equivalent to lending your own funds to the buyer without interest; any default results in a bad debt. Before gran